@startuml
' What: the two clocks (D-39, D-52): ordinary turns for the body, generations for the soul.
' Shows: the generation length L is chosen at game setup (default about 5 turns); pressure piles up turn by turn,
'        normalised to L; a generation starts after L turns or when the pressure crosses a threshold;
'        at the generation change the body is read, the Choice of Fate runs, and the pressure is reset.
' Source: brainstorming-base.md, D-25, D-39, D-48, D-52. Open: threshold and normalisation (Q-48), carry-over instead of reset (Q-47).
title Two clocks: turns and generations (D-39, D-52)
start
:Game setup: generation length L\n(default about 5 turns);
repeat
  repeat
    :Turn: produce, build, research, move, fight;
    :World events and neighbours add pressure p to the lines\n(normalised to L);
    :The profile adds pressure toward each line's current pole;
  repeat while (generation due?\n(L turns, or pressure over threshold)) is (no) not (yes)
  :Generation: read the body, Choice of Fate, profile update;
  :New climate and era policy act until the next generation;
  :Pressure p is reset;
  note right: carry-over (decay) instead of reset: Q-47
repeat while (game goes on?) is (yes) not (no)
stop
@enduml
